// The Overgrown Gate [B, A Inkthread] (bible 8.3): survey the gate and a faded road appears for one night, ending at
// an inn full of Remnant travellers who ask if you've eaten. Gate_2, after the Gatekeeper (6.7). The innkeeper is
// Remnant: half-sentences, present tense, polite; asks if you have eaten; never "I'm dead" (style guide 4).
// And the gate's inscription, environment first (plant 5.6).

title: Gate_Inscription
---
Inscription: Passage for the winged. Land, and be welcome. #plant:5.6 #line:03f23ca
Inscription: Scratched under it, low down, in a hand that climbed: "And the rest of us?" #line:0b9ac87
===

title: Gate_Inn
---
<<if not surveyed("Verdance_Gate_2/Gate")>>
    Inscription: The road ends at the gate. Beyond it, only trees. Nothing is drawn there yet. #still #line:0949e30
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.gate.inn_visited")>>
    Innkeeper: Back. Good. The road is only here the one night. Have you... #still #face:bright #line:0bb15a0
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Innkeeper: A traveller. Come in, come in. The fire is... it is warm. It is warm. #face:bright #line:03ec36e
Innkeeper: Have you eaten? You have not eaten. Sit. #face:bright #line:0847b99
-> Who are all these people? #line:02848e1
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Innkeeper: Travellers. On the road. The road goes to... it goes on. We are waiting for morning. #face:grave #line:07022fd
-> I've eaten, thank you. #line:0578e30
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Innkeeper: Good. Good. Nobody says that. Everyone is so hungry here, and nobody eats. #face:grave #line:0861a94
-> ... #line:07f65e8
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Innkeeper: Tired. Yes. Sit by the... there. The chair knows you. #face:bright #line:01213f0
Innkeeper: In the morning the road goes. It always goes. We are still here, after. Somewhere. #face:grave #line:0e20195
<<flag verdance.gate.inn_visited 1>>
===
